/-! # Cotangent vanishing after quotienting a section differential basis

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 07M7, second paragraph.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-section-differential-basis-quotient).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Algebra

/-- Quotienting by kernel elements whose differentials form a basis along a smooth
section kills both localized cotangent obstructions at every prime along that section.
The quotient and its section are supplied explicitly; no algebra is chosen here.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 07M7, second paragraph, through the vanishing of `H₁`
and `Ω`. (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-section-differential-basis-quotient)

Proof:
1. Put `a = (f₁,...,fₙ)` and `C = D/a`. The smooth Jacobi-Zariski sequence is
   `0 → H₁(L[C/R]) → a/a² → C ⊗[D] Ω[D/R] → Ω[C/R] → 0` and its conormal
   map sends the class of `fᵢ` to `1 ⊗ dfᵢ`.
2. A prime `q` of `C` containing the section kernel pulls back to a prime `p` of `D`
   containing `ker σ`. The map `D → κ(p)` factors through `Q`: the section is
   surjective because the base structure map to `Q` is surjective. The given basis
   therefore becomes a basis over `κ(p)`. The finite projective differential module
   localized at `p` is free of rank `n`, since its residue-field dimension is `n`.
   Consequently `(C ⊗[D] Ω[D/R])_q` is free of rank `n` over `C_q`.
3. Modulo the maximal ideal, the conormal map is surjective by the given basis.
   Nakayama makes it surjective over `C_q`. The source is generated by the `n`
   classes of the `fᵢ`, giving a surjection from `C_q^n` onto it. Compose this with
   the conormal map and a basis identification of the target with `C_q^n`.
   A surjective endomorphism of a finite module is bijective. Thus this composite
   and both maps are bijective, so the localized conormal map is an isomorphism.
4. Localizing the exact sequence is exact. Its kernel and cokernel at that map
   are the displayed localized `H₁` and `Ω`, respectively; both are zero. -/
theorem localized_cotangent_vanishes_of_section_differential_basis
    (R D Q : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing D] [CommRing Q]
    [Algebra R D] [Algebra R Q] [Smooth R D]
    (σ : D →ₐ[R] Q) (hπ : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R Q))
    (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → D) (hf : ∀ i, σ (f i) = 0)
    (hb : letI : Algebra D Q := σ.toRingHom.toAlgebra
      ∃ b : Module.Basis (Fin n) Q (Q ⊗[D] KaehlerDifferential R D),
        ∀ i, b i = 1 ⊗ₜ[D] KaehlerDifferential.D R D (f i))
    (τ : (D ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)) →+* Q)
    (hτ : τ.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f))) = σ.toRingHom) :
    ∀ q : PrimeSpectrum (D ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)),
      RingHom.ker τ ≤ q.asIdeal →
        Subsingleton (LocalizedModule q.asIdeal.primeCompl
          (H1Cotangent R (D ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))) ∧
        Subsingleton (LocalizedModule q.asIdeal.primeCompl
          (KaehlerDifferential R (D ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)))) := by sorry

end Algebra
